  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Iowa federal contracts totaled $63.4M in FY2027 to date. The state recorded 239 awards with an average award size of $265K. Obligations fell 97.0% year over year. Historical context shows larger annual totals before FY2027: FY22 obligations were $3B, FY23 obligations were $4.3B, FY24 obligations were $3.6B, FY25 obligations were $4.7B, and FY26 obligations were $2.1B. The Department of the Treasury is the top buyer in FY2027 to date, obligating $29.3M. PMX INDUSTRIES, INC. is the top vendor in FY2027 to date with $28.2M. Copper Rolling, Drawing, Extruding, and Alloying is the largest NAICS industry by obligations in FY2027 to date with $28.2M. This snapshot covers contract obligations only and reflects fiscal year to date activity rather than a full fiscal year total. Use these figures for procurement planning, prioritizing outreach to the agencies and industries showing the most activity so far in FY2027.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How does FY2027 to date compare with prior fiscal years?",
        "body": "FY27 obligations are $63.4M compared with FY26 obligations of $2.1B. FY25 obligations were $4.7B, FY24 obligations were $3.6B, FY23 obligations were $4.3B, and FY22 obligations were $3B. Obligations fell 97.0% year over year."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies and vendors dominate federal contracting in Iowa so far in FY2027?",
        "body": "The Department of the Treasury obligated $29.3M in FY2027 to date, followed by the Department of Justice with $13.1M and the Department of Veterans Affairs with $9.5M. PMX INDUSTRIES, INC. received $28.2M, ADVANCED TECHNOLOGIES GROUP LLC received $10.9M, and IOWA STATE UNIVERSITY OF SCIENCE AND TECHNOLOGY received $4.4M. Copper Rolling, Drawing, Extruding, and Alloying leads industries with $28.2M."
      }
    ]
  },
