      "q": "How much federal contract money goes to Iowa?",
      "a": "Iowa received $63.4M in federal contract obligations in FY2027 to date. The state recorded 239 awards with an average award size of $265K, and obligations fell 97.0% year over year. Historical annual obligations were larger: FY26 $2.1B, FY25 $4.7B, FY24 $3.6B, FY23 $4.3B, and FY22 $3B."
